<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00568.html">
<title>DSA-6646-1 gpgme1.0 - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00568.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-20</dc:date>
<description>Johan Carlsson discovered that GPGME, a library designed to make access
to GnuPG easier for applications, does not properly handle OpenPGP keys
containing a crafted very long user id, which could result in
information disclosure, denial of service and potentially the execution
of arbitrary code.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6646-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6646-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00567.html">
<title>DSA-6645-1 libgd2 - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00567.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-20</dc:date>
<description>Multiple vulnerabilities were discovered in libgd2, a library for
programmatic graphics creation and manipulation, which could result in
denial of service or information leaks.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6645-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6645-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00566.html">
<title>DSA-6644-1 ruby3.3 - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00566.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-20</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities have been discovered in the interpreter for
the Ruby language, which may result in the execution of arbitrary code.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6644-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6644-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item></rdf:RDF>
